 With 
\begin_inset Formula $D=1+Aa+b>0$
\end_inset

, the price is 
\begin_inset Formula $p=1/D$
\end_inset

, so 
\begin_inset Formula $e=c/D>0$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $c=De$
\end_inset

. This is a one-to-one change of variables for fixed 
\begin_inset Formula $A,b,F$
\end_inset

 and a given 
\begin_inset Formula $a$
\end_inset

. Substitution gives 
\begin_inset Formula \[
f(e,a,r;A,b)=-\frac{1}{De}-\frac{a}{8}+r,\qquad e+r\le2-F,\quad e>0,\quad a,r\ge0.
\]
\end_inset

The feasible set is convex. The objective is concave in all choices and strictly concave in 
\begin_inset Formula $(e,a)$
\end_inset

. Thus a feasible point with a valid KKT certificate is a global optimum. Budget exhaustion determines 
\begin_inset Formula $r$
\end_inset

; strict concavity then gives uniqueness of the full optimum.
\end_layout

