\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Method 1: numeraire normalization and entry screening.
\series default
 With a positive numeraire, set 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda=1$
\end_inset

 and use only 
\begin_inset Formula \[
e=D^{-1/2},\qquad E_{a}=AD^{-3/2}-\frac{1}{8}\le0,\qquad aE_{a}=0.
\]
\end_inset

At 
\begin_inset Formula $a=0$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $D=1+b$
\end_inset

. Entry has positive surplus if 
\begin_inset Formula $1+b<(8A)^{2/3}$
\end_inset

, so that boundary is rejected. Otherwise the boundary passes. A positive-search candidate requires 
\begin_inset Formula $D=(8A)^{2/3}$
\end_inset

. Recover 
\begin_inset Formula $\mu=-E_{a}$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\eta=0$
\end_inset

. At the threshold the entry surplus is zero, not strictly negative: uniqueness follows from the global certificate. This method is the shortest route to the comparative table; no full second KKT calculation is needed for each case.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Method 2: budget reduction and one-dimensional optimization.
\series default
 Set 
\begin_inset Formula $r=2-F-e$
\end_inset

, retaining 
\begin_inset Formula $0<e\le2-F$
\end_inset

. Write 
\begin_inset Formula $d=1+b$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $a=(D-d)/A$
\end_inset

, so 
\begin_inset Formula $D\ge d$
\end_inset

. Maximization is equivalent to minimizing 
\begin_inset Formula \[
J(e,D)=e+\frac{1}{De}+\frac{D-d}{8A}.
\]
\end_inset

For a fixed 
\begin_inset Formula $D$
\end_inset

, the sharp inequality 
\begin_inset Formula \[
e+\frac{1}{De}\ge\frac{2}{\sqrt{D}},\qquad e+\frac{1}{De}-\frac{2}{\sqrt{D}}=\frac{(e-D^{-1/2})^{2}}{e}
\]
\end_inset

gives the unique minimizing expenditure. It must satisfy the retained wealth constraint, which holds in (c) and for the contracts in (d). The remaining derivative is 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\frac{d}{dD}\left(\frac{2}{\sqrt{D}}+\frac{D-d}{8A}\right)=\frac{1}{8A}-D^{-3/2}.
\]
\end_inset

Thus 
\begin_inset Formula $D^{*}=\max\{(8A)^{2/3},d\}$
\end_inset

. Recover 
\begin_inset Formula $a,e,c,p,r$
\end_inset

. This route is global. The explicit KKT system is still required in (b), and a zero-effort check is still required in (c).
\end_layout

